<h1>Agent 1: empirical dimensionality reduction</h1>
<p>BIOS 774 · Local reproducible statistical agent · Scientific wording is a draft for user review.</p>
<h2>Problem and contribution</h2>
<p>A useful dimensionality-reduction workflow should explain why a method advances on the dataset at hand. This agent inspects numerical data, chooses explicit preprocessing, attempts all supported methods on a common pilot, and uses measured quality, stability, failures, and runtime to select a small final candidate set. It then tunes only that shortlist and produces auditable reports.</p>
<h2>Architecture and tools</h2>
<p>A Python src package exposes inspect → pilot → select → tune → final → report → validate through one CLI and run-all. Typed configuration, atomic JSON artifacts, content checksums and subprocess isolation make stages resumable. SLURM supplies CPU execution; Python scientific packages implement numerical tools. Jinja2 and WeasyPrint generate PDFs, checked with pypdf. No multi-agent framework, web service or database is required.</p>
<p>All ten methods are real implementations: PCA, Kernel PCA, MDS, Isomap, LLE, Laplacian Eigenmaps, Diffusion Maps, Bayesian GPLVM, t-SNE and UMAP. Scikit-learn supplies seven, pydiffmap supplies diffusion maps, GPyTorch optimizes Bayesian GPLVM, and umap-learn supplies UMAP. The GPLVM loss and changes from PCA initialization are recorded.</p>
<h2>Dataset-aware planning and decision logic</h2>
<p>PBMC count data undergo fixed cell QC, cohort-specific gene filtering, library normalization, log transformation, variable-gene selection, and scaling. PathMNIST uses consistently scaled RGB pixels. Cohorts are stratified where annotations exist, while all fitting and selection exclude labels. A cohort-fitted PCA representation supplies identical numerical input to every method.</p>
<p>Quality combines trustworthiness (weight 0.45), nearest-neighbor recall (0.45), and seed stability (0.10). Methods meeting 90% of the best quality or on the quality–runtime Pareto frontier are eligible; candidates are ranked by quality, runtime, then name. Successful PCA is retained as the baseline, with at most four finalists. Severe connectivity or singularity warnings exclude a method. All original warnings and failures remain visible.</p>
<p>Stochastic methods have repeated seeds; deterministic stability is defined as one. Shortlist refinement uses the same criteria. Silhouette is secondary. These are descriptive in-cohort analyses; there is no held-out inference claim.</p>
