<div class="page"></div><h1>Assessment and reproducibility</h1>
<h2>Strengths and limits</h2>
<p>The same public interface adapts to sparse count data and dense images, with transparent common-cohort comparisons and quantitative candidate selection. Traceable artifacts preserve failed attempts and numerical warnings instead of presenting only attractive embeddings. Runtime-aware cohort planning makes expensive methods feasible under a declared budget.</p>
<p>Results depend on representation, metric weights, neighborhood scale and random seeds. Local metrics do not fully measure global structure. Deterministic methods receive a defined stability value; this is not proof of robustness to resampling. GPLVM uses a fixed optimization budget and may need longer training. Disconnected graph warnings conservatively exclude methods. Cold-start imports affect runtime, and cubic planning bounds are conservative assumptions rather than measured scaling laws.</p>
<p>PathMNIST pixel distances need not reflect all histological semantics. PBMC processed labels originate from prior clustering and do not provide independent biological ground truth. No causal, clinical or generalization conclusion follows from the embeddings. Neither source is sent to an external model in deterministic mode.</p>
<h2>Reproduction and audit</h2>
<p>Run scripts/01_setup_environment.sh for the exact agent environment, then scripts/03_smoke_test.sh inside a SLURM allocation. Stage scripts in scripts/slurm accept a dataset config. Run python -m agent1_dr run-all --config config/pbmc3k.yaml --resume and the analogous PathMNIST command on compute nodes. Finally run project-report and validate --all-reports. The lock files, configuration/code hashes, source checksums, cohort IDs, seeds, and job manifests specify the evidence chain.</p>
<p>Three PDFs are generated from validated artifacts. The default mode is deterministic templating, not an LLM-written report. An optional OpenAI interface can organize exact evidence sentences and rejects unsupported claims; live API operation requires credentials. Tests exercise the actual methods, GPLVM optimization, failure isolation, metric behavior, selection and a fresh end-to-end synthetic run.</p>
